.TH ZXKIT\-MC\-SETUP 1 "November 2026" "zxkit" "ZxKit"
.SH NAME
zxkit\-mc\-setup \- enable ZX Spectrum image support in Midnight Commander
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zxkit\-mc\-setup
.RB [ \-\-remove ]
.RB [ \-\-user\-file
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-\-system\-file
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-\-fragment
.IR FILE ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Adds the ZxKit file associations to the user's Midnight Commander extension
file, so that Enter opens a ZX Spectrum tape, disk or Microdrive image as an
archive and F3 lists it.
The extfs helper itself works without this command once it is in Midnight
Commander's extfs directory (for example
.I /usr/lib/mc/extfs.d
on Debian, or
.I ~/.local/share/mc/extfs.d
for one user): type
.B cd games.tap/zxkit://
in a panel.
.PP
Midnight Commander reads a single extension file, and the user's
.I ~/.config/mc/mc.ext.ini
replaces the system file
.I /etc/mc/mc.ext.ini
completely.
When the user has no file yet, it is created from a copy of the system file.
The ZxKit sections are kept between the lines
.B # BEGIN ZxKit (zxkit\-mc\-setup)
and
.BR "# END ZxKit (zxkit\-mc\-setup)" ,
so running the command again, for example after an upgrade, replaces them and
leaves the rest of the file alone.
The file must be in the
.B mc.ext.ini
4.0 format of Midnight Commander 4.8.29 and later;
any other file is left unchanged and reported.
Restart Midnight Commander afterwards.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-remove
Take the ZxKit sections out again.
.TP
.BI \-\-user\-file " FILE"
The extension file to change.
The default is
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/mc/mc.ext.ini
or
.IR ~/.config/mc/mc.ext.ini .
.TP
.BI \-\-system\-file " FILE"
The file to start from when there is no user file.
The default is the first of
.I /etc/mc/mc.ext.ini
and
.IR /usr/share/mc/mc.ext.ini .
.TP
.BI \-\-fragment " FILE"
The sections to add.
The default is the installed
.IR zxkit.ini ,
.I share/zxkit/mc/zxkit.ini
under the install prefix, or the one next to the script in a source checkout.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 when the extension file cannot be used or written and 2 for a
usage error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mc (1),
.BR zxmedia (1)
